Messages: {
	BossNotImplemented: Whatever this would call has not been written yet - nothing answers.
	BossAlreadyActive: It is already here.
	BossSummoned: Signal sent. It is on its way.
	FireplaceOpened: The Fireplace's lockdown protocol has been lifted - the entrance is open.
	TerminalRead: The old-world data terminal still hums... fragmented records are read out.
	FirstMemoryRestored: Machina recovered her first memory - the Watchman Project shares its origin with the Scavenger.
	ScavengerPhaseTwo: Scavenger - Overload Repair protocol engaged - summoning repair drones.
	ScavengerPhaseThree: Scavenger - sensor array shattered. Indiscriminate purge in progress.
	ScavengerOverload: Scavenger - core overload - self-destructive charge imminent!
	ScavengerSelfDestruct: Scavenger - chassis disintegrating.
	ScavengerWarning: A piercing screech seems to ring at the edge of hearing, and the air reeks of blood...
	ScavengerArrived: The Scavenger has arrived - it has judged everything here as pollution.
	ScavengerSummoned: Signal sent. The Scavenger has locked onto your position.
	ScavengerAlreadyActive: A Scavenger is already carrying out its purge protocol.
	ScavengerWrecked: The Scavenger tore itself apart in overload - nothing usable remains.
	CoreReceived: You wake with a cold core in your palm - it is still beating.
	FrameNeedsCore: This body is hollow. Perhaps a core could fill it.
	CompanionAwakened: The core settles into the body - she opens her eyes.
	CompanionArrived: Machina {0} has arrived.
	CompanionAlreadyHere: She is already awake.
	ArchivistPhaseTwo: Archivist - reindexing complete. Filing protocol engaged.
	ArchivistPhaseThree: Archivist - overwrite authorised. Your path has been archived.
	ArchivistSuppression: Archivist - terminal lockdown. Nothing leaves the archive.
	ArchivistDefeated: The audit unit comes apart into loose pages - one archived log is left behind.
	SecondMemoryRestored: Machina recovered her second memory - the mass-produced units were blanked on purpose.
	ArchivistSealed: An archiving seal has been placed - you are pinned in place.
	AshHeartPhaseTwo: Ash Heart - the burn sustains itself. Wisps are feeding the core.
	AshHeartPhaseThree: Ash Heart - collapse. The pulse is pulling inward.
	AshHeartDefeated: The Heart breaks open. The war order is still warm.
	ThirdMemoryRestored: Machina recovered her third memory - she wrote the burn, and she carried it out.
	FireplaceGuardianPhaseTwo: Fireplace Guardian - cold ignition. The ring is closing.
	FireplaceGuardianPhaseThree: Fireplace Guardian - reset protocol. The walls are coming in.
	FireplaceGuardianDefeated: The last lock opens. The reset device is waiting for a carrier.
	FourthMemoryRestored: Machina recovered her fourth memory. The Fireplace was never a shelter.
	TrueName: She remembers the name this body had. Elvi.
	EndingVessel: She will carry the reset. This world still walks to its end. The next dawn will know her.
	EndingRefuse: She will not be the weapon again. The world still ends, but not by her hand.
	CodaVessel: The Moon Lord falls. The reset she carries kindles. Somewhere else, a first morning starts.
	CodaRefuse: The Moon Lord falls. The stars go out on schedule. Her name does not.
	EnteredFireplace: The air changes. You are inside the Fireplace.
	TerminalTalkToHer: The terminal has read you a broken log. Bring it back to her.
	GatePlaced: A warm door has opened near where you woke. The Fireplace is listening.
	FireplaceEnterFailed: The door is here, but the way through did not open. Subworld Library has to be enabled.
}

Dialogue: {
	MechanicalCompanion: {
		ButtonStory: Story
		ButtonMemory: Memory Fragments
		Intro1: ...You came back. Though I can't remember how long I waited.
		Intro2: My memory starts inside a field of static. Only one thing is clear - I had to find you before the Fireplace goes out.
		Intro3: This body was salvaged from an elven ruin. The old world built it beautifully, then never told it how to live.
		Intro4: Those moving things outside are all labeled "pollution" in my program. Don't ask me why - that one line is all my log has left.
		AfterScavenger1: Execution Unit-07 has stopped functioning. Strange. I should be glad, yet my data is shaking.
		AfterScavenger2: It came from the same blueprint as you and me - only its thinking module was deleted. Who deleted it?
		AfterScavenger3: The Fireplace entrance is open. The old terminal is still running inside. Perhaps it can tell me what I am.
		Memory4: Fourth memory: the fireplace was never a shelter. It is a reset device. The old world never intended to survive; it only intended to begin again.
		Memory2: Second memory: the mass-produced units were not built broken - they were left blank on purpose. And the code in that log, the part signed Archived... carries my own serial number.
		Memory3: Third memory: I recognise every pulse of the Ash Heart. I wrote that war program. The one who carried it out was not it - it was me.
		AfterMemory1: The first memory is back. I am the prototype of the Watchman Project - the Scavenger is my mass-produced model.
		AfterMemory2: The mass-produced units had their capacity for thought deliberately cut away, leaving only the kill order. So... is the one who wrote that order a murderer?
		AfterMemory3: There is a section of code in my log marked "Archived". I cannot open it, but I can feel it watching me.
		StoryHunt: Go find the execution unit still sweeping. It wanders outside the Fireplace, judging everything alive as pollution. Its code reads - weakened = heavily polluted. So it will lunge at whoever is hurt the worst.
		StoryFireplace: The Fireplace door is open. It was the old world's last shelter, and the only target written into my protection list. Go look at the data terminal inside.
		StoryTerminalRead: I have already read the terminal's fragmented data. I can try to piece it back into my memory - but be sure you truly want the answer.
		StoryAfterMemory: The next memory needs a stronger vessel to hold it. Keep growing stronger - three more "Archives" are waiting out there.
		MemoryBlank: Memory fragments - none. My storage holds nothing but static, and one instruction repeating - protect the Fireplace.
		MemoryFirst: ...Read successful. "Watchman Project" - mass-produce execution units from the prototype's template to purge everything outside the Fireplace. I am that prototype. The Scavenger is my mass-produced model - its thinking module was deliberately deleted, so it cannot even ask "why".
		MemoryUnstable: The data is becoming unstable. Some fragments are not mine, yet they are taking root in my storage.
		MemoryRecovered: Memory fragments - 1 / 4 recovered. The rest are still "Archived". Don't rush - I am not sure I want to know all of it.
		AfterArchivist1: Something found me. It was not hunting the body - it was hunting my logs. It called itself an audit unit.
		AfterArchivist2: It sealed one section back up before it died. My serial number is written on that seal. Why would an auditor be sent after me?
		MemorySecondNeedFragment: You brought something back from it, didn't you. Give it to me - I will read it. I have to know what it filed about me.
		MemorySecond: ...Read successful. The mass-produced units were not built broken. Their capacity to think was cut away on purpose - and the code that signed off on the cut, the section marked "Archived"... carries my own serial number.
		MemoryRecovered2: Memory fragments - 2 / 4 recovered. The next one is buried deeper. I am starting to think I was not a witness. I was a participant.
		StoryAwaitSecond: The audit unit is still out there. Find out what it filed about me - and bring it back. Then I can read the second memory.
		StoryAfterSecondMemory: Two memories left, and both are sealed behind things that were built to guard them. Keep growing stronger. The next archive does not audit - it burns.
		AfterSecondMemory1: I wrote a line of code once, long ago. I cannot see what it did, but my storage flinches whenever I reach for it.
		AfterSecondMemory2: The audit unit is gone, but the section it resealed is still there, quietly pulling the rest of my logs out of order.
		AfterSecondMemory3: If I was the one who signed that order... then asking "who deleted their thinking module" was the wrong question all along.
		AfterAsh1: I can feel it from here. Something underground is still burning, and it knows my serial number.
		AfterAsh2: Don't stand in the ash. It is not leftover. It is still following an order.
		AfterThird1: I wrote the burn. Saying it out loud does not make it smaller.
		AfterThird2: The next lock is not outside. It is sitting in the Fireplace, waiting for someone to finish me.
		AfterFourth1: Elvi. That was the name of the body, before the core. I think I want to keep it.
		AfterFourth2: The reset needs a carrier. If I step in, this world still ends - but the next one starts with a person instead of a protocol.
		EndingVessel1: I am holding the dawn shut until this world is finished. Stay with me until then.
		EndingVessel2: Don't thank me. I am not saving this place. I am making sure the next one is not born empty.
		EndingRefuse1: I will watch it end. I will not be the hand that ends it.
		EndingRefuse2: Zero was a serial number. Elvi can just be a person who stayed.
		ButtonTrade: Trade
		ButtonVessel: Carry the reset
		ButtonRefuse: Refuse
		StoryHuntAsh: The next archive burns. It is a heart that never went out, somewhere the world is already rotten. Bring me what is left of it.
		StoryBringThird: You broke the Heart. If you found the cinder that still has my handwriting, give it to me.
		StoryHuntGuardian: The last lock is inside the Fireplace. It is not a monster. It is the door, refusing to open until someone is willing to be the key.
		StoryBringFourth: The Guardian is down. The last fragment has my name in it. I need to read it myself.
		StoryChoice: Two ways through. I become the carrier of the reset, or I stay Elvi and let the world end without using me again. Both of them still end this place.
		StoryEndingVessel: I chose the dawn. When the last lord of this moon falls, the reset I am holding will kindle somewhere else.
		StoryEndingRefuse: I chose the name. When the sky finally goes dark, it will not be because I signed another order.
		MemoryThirdNeedFragment: The Heart broke, but I cannot read a fire from memory alone. Bring me the fragment.
		MemoryThird: ...Read successful. Watchman burn protocol, signed by the prototype. The mass-produced units killed what I marked. The Ash Heart is the mark I left, and I was the one who carried the order out.
		MemoryFourthNeedFragment: The lock is open. The fragment is the only copy of my name. Give it here.
		MemoryFourth: ...Read successful. The Fireplace is a reset device. The old world did not plan to survive. It planned to begin again, using the prototype as the carrier. The body I am wearing had a name before the core. Elvi.
		ChoiceVessel: Then I will carry it. Not to save this world. To make sure the next one wakes up with someone in it.
		ChoiceRefuse: Then I stay. The world can end on its own. I will not sign the order a second time.
	}

	// 四首 Boss 曲的显示名：tModLoader 按 Mods.<模组>.Music.<文件名> 取名字，
	// 所以键名必须和 Music/ 下的文件名一致（Scavenger / Archivist / AshHeart / FireplaceGuardian）
	Music: {
		Scavenger: Execution Unit-07
		Archivist: The Audit Unit
		AshHeart: The Heart That Never Went Out
		FireplaceGuardian: The Last Door
	}
}
